    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>That's a pretty strong stance. It sounds like you're saying there wasn't really much of a downside to all that union power, or that the economic disruptions and stuff didn't really matter compared to the gains? I've heard some people argue that union monopolies actually hurt productivity or made things more expensive for everyone else. How do you view those critiques?",
